  "vegSub": "Regional Ecosystems 12.1.1 / 12.3.6 · Casuarina glauca forest on estuarine margins, with Melaleuca quinquenervia–Blue Gum–Swamp Box forest on the coastal plain · Southeast Queensland",
  "intro": "Before 1750 your address sat where Moreton Bay's tidal edge met the low coastal plain. On the wettest, saltiest ground stood Swamp She-oak forest with Broad-leaved Paperbark; a little higher grew open paperbark forest with Queensland Blue Gum, Swamp Box and Pink Bloodwood over a grassy, sedgy floor that flooded each wet season. It is koala country and frog country, and it filters water on its way to the bay. Swamp She-oak forest is now listed as Of Concern. The plants below are indigenous to these two communities and grouped by the layer they fill. Plant the canopy first; the lilies, ferns, sedges and grasses belong in the damp light beneath it.",
